        "original_id": "1a41d465-80e3-5a03-84f3-f4fb1d59e91b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Grindé, Karel Reisz, Tony Richardson\n- Works: Saturday Night and Sunday Morning\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, filmmaker, producer\n- Topics: British cinema, new realism\n\nFacts:\n- Nick Grindé was born on January 12, 1893, and he was an American film director and screenwriter.\n- Karel Reisz was born on July 21, 1926, and he became a British filmmaker active in post-World War II Britain.\n- Karel Reisz was one of the pioneers of the new realist strain in British cinema during the 1950s and 1960s.\n- Saturday Night and Sunday Morning is a 1960 British drama film directed by Karel Reisz and produced by Tony Richardson.\n- Nick Grindé died on June 19, 1979.\n- Karel Reisz died on November 25, 2002.",
